*** ch13-15-assoc-id — associative with identity (AU) unification: irredundant unify yields the 3-element minimal set (plain unify would give 32) (Maude manual §13.4.7)
*** PRELUDE

fmod UNIFICATION-EX5 is
 protecting NAT .
 sort NList .
 op nil : -> NList .
 subsort Nat < NList .
 op _:_ : NList NList -> NList [assoc id: nil] .
endfm

irredundant unify in UNIFICATION-EX5 :
      X:NList : Y:NList : Z:NList =? P:NList : Q:NList .
